    "recommendations": "• Mark the entrance to each access drive with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Post structure identification markers on each detached structure so responders can quickly distinguish buildings during an incident.\n• Keep both access drives clear of parked vehicles and equipment to allow full-length drive-through access.\n• Clear the equipment storage area of any items that extend into either access drive or the vehicle parking area.\n• Mark or identify which access drive provides the most direct route to the rear of the property for responding units.\n• Maintain a minimum turning radius in the vehicle parking area so emergency apparatus can reposition without backing into unknown terrain.\n• Install a gate or barrier marker at the point where paved or improved surface ends and open terrain begins to prevent responders from driving into soft or uneven ground.\n• Identify and mark the nearest point of rear access so responders arriving for the first time can locate it without searching.\n• Keep the vehicle parking area free of stored equipment so it can serve as a staging area for responding units.\n• Trim any vegetation along both access drives that reduces vertical clearance or side clearance for larger emergency vehicles."
  },
