    "recommendations": "• Move wood piles away from the outer walls of structures in the cluster.\n• Thin scattered shrubs that sit close to any structure in the cluster.\n• Trim lower branches on large trees that hang directly over or near rooftops.\n• Keep grass areas near the structure cluster mowed short, especially during dry periods.\n• Clear a turning area near the structure cluster so vehicles can reverse direction without backing long distances.\n• Remove dead or dry grass buildup that has collected beneath shrubs near structures.\n• Separate any wood piles from nearby shrubs or grass cover by several feet of bare ground.\n• Trim overhanging branches along access routes to keep them clear for vehicles."
